{"parentUuid":null,"isSidechain":true,"promptId":"69fd3a36-77b0-4682-8147-3d9be25bf8f4","agentId":"ae420e7134ad1bf48","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"Repo C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers. Python .venv\\Scripts\\python.exe. No subagents, never open COM3; TestClient + fixtures (copy the 2026-10-13 lines from C:\\ProgramData\\cuore\\observations.jsonl at test time; never modify it). At most 10 check suites, only those your files touch; no re-runs of suites that passed. Report under 150 words. An integration agent is running the full suite and may commit; re-read any file before editing and keep edits focused. Do NOT edit job.html/job.js/job.css/_flow_bar.html/_vtabs.html (a second agent gets the UI items next). You may commit and push (`github` main only; never koch-mcp/).\n\nApply the LOGIC items of docs/research/EXTERNAL_REVIEW_6_2026-10-14.md (read once):\n1. One data date, one truth: from-car observations (obd_dtcs, module_dtcs, readiness, mode06, freeze_frame, pid) must be treated as scan sessions by the workup/clear-assessment and the Codes page, so \"returned -- erased and set again\" is computed for P0440/P0455 (cleared 8 Oct 09:20 by MES, read back stored 13 Oct 20:03 from the car), the header/Report \"data through\" date becomes 2026-10-13, and Codes/step 4 state matches the Verdict (ACTIVE, not CLEARED_UNVERIFIED). Likely files: mes-log-mcp/mes/workup.py (+analysis), cuore/services/dossier_bridge.py, mes_bridge, the Codes route. Also: step 5 \"No active codes to explain\" and step 1 \"(no complaint recorded)\" must derive from the same sources as the verdict/symptoms store (jobs_bridge/flow_bridge); U1736 must appear in the Codes list (live-only codes included); C1408-86 consistent between Codes/Systems and the job chassis group; the Bench \"KOEO BLOCKED: MES running\" must use the same mes_state as the \"Scanner:\" label.\n2. Fuel gate: the EVAP gate value must come from the newest from-car PID 2F read (20.8 % on 13 Oct) when present, else the newest freeze frame, ALWAYS with timestamp + source next to it; when the value is older than the latest readiness read the gate becomes a warning (\"fuel level last read <date>; verify before trusting the monitor\") not a block (bench_bridge, tests_bridge, dossier_bridge).\n3. Mode $06 limits: the decoder/renderers print \"vs min 0 ms\" for a test whose limit is a max (TID 90: 6096 vs 0..6000). Render \"value 6096 ms, limit max 6000 ms -- FAIL\" using whichever bound was exceeded; verify the min/max assignment in cuore/live/mode06.py against SAE J1979 (min/max order in the 6-byte record) and fix if swapped; health report and Scans use the same text.\n4. Evidence: freeze frames flagged \"above 85 %: monitor could not run\" are test-condition items, never auto-listed as evidence FOR a hypothesis (label them \"conditions\" in the picker); recorded test results (step 6 rows with pass/fail, Tests-surface results, Mode $06 FAILs from the car) must appear in the \"+ Evidence for/against\" picker and the step-6 result sheet must let the mechanic pick OR create a hypothesis inline from the suggested list (jobs_bridge + the API; the template change in job.html is for the UI agent -- expose the data and a POST that accepts hypothesis_text to create-and-link). Honour the Tests page's auto-attach promise: a Tests result with a hypothesis_id attaches; without one it offers the pick.\n5. Knowledge: split the Body group so mechanical B-codes (B1176 window regulator) are not grouped with comms codes; C104B (ABS hydraulic leak) gets a direct brake-fluid level / hydraulic-leak inspection step from mechanic_tests (brake hydraulic test exists) instead of electrical-only steps; single-session codes older than 180 days with no return are demoted from open work to history (rule in the open-work builder, documented). Add the flooded-canister path as a sourced hypothesis/test if TSB 9100471 is on file (grep mes for 9100471 once; if absent, add the TSB reference as UNKNOWN-sourced note, do not invent its content).\nTests for each. Commit \"Review 6 logic: live reads are scan sessions (returned computed, one data date), fuel gate from the newest read with source, Mode 06 limit wording, evidence picker includes results, body/brake/stale-code rules\" with the Co-Authored-By line, push, report hash."},"uuid":"e0fc9a38-0e0a-4753-b992-b42a81f85998","timestamp":"2026-10-14T12:06:39.092Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
