{"parentUuid":"4ae43cc6-c342-4da9-b058-ee53cae185b5","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"ae420e7134ad1bf48","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Cg27Dqc7fiHGDnkxrHF4h","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XXYZLaBTU7b9CS2cJL7zno","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\cuore\\services\\bench_bridge.py","offset":1,"limit":135},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1176,"cache_read_input_tokens":162214,"output_tokens":947,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":826},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1176},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":947,"cache_read_input_tokens":162214,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1176,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1176,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01XXYZLaBTU7b9CS2cJL7zno":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\cuore\\services\\bench_bridge.py","offset":1,"limit":135}},"serverClassifierRequest":"9be941c8-ce94-48b0-b16e-6421dee1941a","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cg27DqGWiWyqEjc7qY8xA","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"ad5b41e5-473d-403e-8eac-62cd28098441","timestamp":"2026-10-14T12:12:15.375Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"ad5b41e5-473d-403e-8eac-62cd28098441","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"69fd3a36-77b0-4682-8147-3d9be25bf8f4","agentId":"ae420e7134ad1bf48","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XXYZLaBTU7b9CS2cJL7zno","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\"\"\"Data for the bench page: \"what am I doing to this car, right now\".\n2\t\n3\t``cuore/web/routes.py``'s old ``/v/{vin}`` was the full dossier -- verdict,\n4\tevery code, every bulletin, every freeze frame, all at once. That page still\n5\texists (moved to ``/v/{vin}/dossier``); this module backs the thing a\n6\tmechanic actually wants the instant the car is on the lift: a resume\n7\tsummary of what changed since the last visit, the verdict's own next-action\n8\tsentence, the tasks to go do about it (with procedure, pass criteria, parts\n9\tand tools each one needs already resolved), live preconditions, the fuel\n10\tgate and readiness panel, and a couple of jump-off points (codes, the job,\n11\tthe full dossier) -- nothing that needs scrolling to reach on a 400x800\n12\tscreen.\n13\t\n14\t``build_bench`` is the only entry point. It composes bridges that already\n15\texist -- ``dossier_bridge.build_view`` for the verdict/open-work/codes/\n16\tbulletins/freeze-frames, ``mes_bridge.fault_tree`` for sourced procedure\n17\tsteps, ``electrical_bridge`` for electrical/physical inspect steps,\n18\t``known_good_bridge`` for expected readings, ``parts_bridge``/\n19\t``tools_kb_bridge`` for what a step needs, ``cuore.live.ops``/``checklists``\n20\tfor live status and the shop-ticked checklist, ``shop_bridge``/\n21\t``cases_bridge`` for the header line and the case hint -- and invents no new\n22\tdiagnosis of its own. See BENCH_UX_SPEC_2026-10-08.md for the walkthrough\n23\tthis module answers.\n24\t\"\"\"\n25\t\n26\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n27\t\n28\timport json\n29\timport re\n30\timport threading\n31\tfrom collections import Counter\n32\tfrom datetime import datetime\n33\tfrom pathlib import Path\n34\tfrom typing import Any\n35\t\n36\tfrom . import cache, dossier_bridge, known_good_bridge, mes_bridge, parts_bridge, tools_kb_bridge\n37\tfrom .errors import BadRequest\n38\tfrom ..live import checklists as checklist_store\n39\tfrom ..live.config import state_dir\n40\t\n41\ttry:\n42\t    from . import cases_bridge\n43\texcept Exception:  # noqa: BLE001 -- the bench must still render without it\n44\t    cases_bridge = None\n45\t\n46\ttry:\n47\t    from . import shop_bridge\n48\texcept Exception:  # noqa: BLE001\n49\t    shop_bridge = None\n50\t\n51\ttry:\n52\t    from . import electrical_bridge\n53\texcept Exception:  # noqa: BLE001\n54\t    electrical_bridge = None\n55\t\n56\ttry:\n57\t    from ..live import ops as live_ops\n58\texcept Exception:  # noqa: BLE001\n59\t    live_ops = None\n60\t\n61\ttry:\n62\t    from . import scanlog_bridge\n63\texcept Exception:  # noqa: BLE001\n64\t    scanlog_bridge = None\n65\t\n66\t\n67\t#: Capped the same way the spec caps each bench card: 3 next actions, each\n68\t#: with at most 3 parts and 4 tools.\n69\t_MAX_ACTIONS = 3\n70\t_MAX_PARTS = 3\n71\t_MAX_TOOLS = 4\n72\t_MAX_SHORTCUTS = 6\n73\t_MAX_INSPECT_STEPS = 4\n74\t\n75\t#: Hours since the newest scan/session before the bench flags it stale\n76\t#: (BENCH_UX_SPEC_2026-10-08.md A2) -- a stale read silently invalidates the\n77\t#: whole checklist, so this is surfaced on the bench itself, not just in the\n78\t#: dossier footer.\n79\t_STALE_HOURS = 24.0\n80\t\n81\t#: Family key (lowercased, as ``dossier_bridge.FAMILY_STEPS``/the generic\n82\t#: SAE-range rules spell it) -> icon registry key, for the bench card's own\n83\t#: pictogram. Anything not listed here falls back to a generic glyph --\n84\t#: never a 500 for a family this table doesn't know about yet.\n85\tFAMILY_ICON: dict[str, str] = {\n86\t    \"evap\": \"sys_evap\", \"network\": \"sys_network\", \"misfire\": \"sys_ignition\",\n87\t    \"fuel_trim\": \"sys_fuel\", \"cooling\": \"sys_cooling\",\n88\t    \"engine_management\": \"sys_engine_management\",\n89\t    \"transmission_driveline\": \"sys_transmission_driveline\", \"adas\": \"sys_adas_sensors\",\n90\t    \"chassis\": \"sys_suspension\", \"body\": \"sys_body_comfort\",\n91\t    \"powertrain_other\": \"sys_engine_management\",\n92\t}\n93\t\n94\t#: The chip colour legend rendered once below the DTC shortcut chips\n95\t#: (BENCH_UX_SPEC_2026-10-08.md D11) -- kept here, not guessed per-chip in\n96\t#: the template, so the legend and the chip classes can never drift apart.\n97\t_STATUS_LEGEND = [\n98\t    {\"label\": \"Active\", \"css\": \"v-active\"},\n99\t    {\"label\": \"Cleared, unverified\", \"css\": \"v-cleared-unverified\"},\n100\t]\n101\t\n102\t#: JOB_UX_FIXES_2026-10-08.md item 9: a single source of human labels for\n103\t#: every raw enum this module's own output otherwise carries, so a template\n104\t#: never has to show (or re-invent a translation for) a bare value like\n105\t#: ``not_running`` or a verdict ``blocker`` key. Every other enum this page\n106\t#: shows (verdict state/label, tool ``have``) is already human-labelled at\n107\t#: its own source (dossier_bridge/tools_kb_bridge) -- this dict only covers\n108\t#: the two that weren't: the live MES/scanner state, and the one-line\n109\t#: action for each ``blocker`` key :func:`_fuel_gate`/the verdict compute.\n110\tLABELS: dict[str, dict[str, str]] = {\n111\t    \"mes_state\": {\n112\t        \"connected\": \"Connected\", \"disconnected\": \"Disconnected\",\n113\t        \"not_running\": \"Not running\", \"unknown\": \"Unknown\",\n114\t    },\n115\t    \"blocker\": {\n116\t        \"fuel out of window\": \"Burn fuel to 15-85 %, then run a drive cycle.\",\n117\t        \"awaiting drive cycle\": \"Run a drive cycle, then read readiness.\",\n118\t        \"active faults\": \"Open the codes and start the first test below.\",\n119\t    },\n120\t}\n121\t\n122\t\n123\tdef scanner_label(live_status: dict[str, Any]) -> str:\n124\t    \"\"\"\"Connected\" / \"Not running\" / ... -- never the raw MES state enum,\n125\t    never \"MES ?\" for an unreadable strip.\"\"\"\n126\t    if live_status.get(\"error\"):\n127\t        return \"Unknown\"\n128\t    return LABELS[\"mes_state\"].get(live_status.get(\"mes_state\"), \"Unknown\")\n129\t\n130\t\n131\tdef _blocker_banner(verdict: dict[str, Any]) -> dict[str, Any] | None:\n132\t    \"\"\"The ONE banner the bench shows for \"what do I do right now\" (item\n133\t    17): an icon, a short one-line action, and the verdict's own full\n134\t    sentence + basis behind \"Why?\". ``None`` only when there is no\n135\t    next_action sentence at all (should not happen in practice)."}]},"uuid":"2e1bd3a0-3fe7-4be2-b062-1295b6fb4953","timestamp":"2026-10-14T12:12:15.419Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\cuore\\services\\bench_bridge.py","content":"\"\"\"Data for the bench page: \"what am I doing to this car, right now\".\n\n``cuore/web/routes.py``'s old ``/v/{vin}`` was the full dossier -- verdict,\nevery code, every bulletin, every freeze frame, all at once. That page still\nexists (moved to ``/v/{vin}/dossier``); this module backs the thing a\nmechanic actually wants the instant the car is on the lift: a resume\nsummary of what changed since the last visit, the verdict's own next-action\nsentence, the tasks to go do about it (with procedure, pass criteria, parts\nand tools each one needs already resolved), live preconditions, the fuel\ngate and readiness panel, and a couple of jump-off points (codes, the job,\nthe full dossier) -- nothing that needs scrolling to reach on a 400x800\nscreen.\n\n``build_bench`` is the only entry point. It composes bridges that already\nexist -- ``dossier_bridge.build_view`` for the verdict/open-work/codes/\nbulletins/freeze-frames, ``mes_bridge.fault_tree`` for sourced procedure\nsteps, ``electrical_bridge`` for electrical/physical inspect steps,\n``known_good_bridge`` for expected readings, ``parts_bridge``/\n``tools_kb_bridge`` for what a step needs, ``cuore.live.ops``/``checklists``\nfor live status and the shop-ticked checklist, ``shop_bridge``/\n``cases_bridge`` for the header line and the case hint -- and invents no new\ndiagnosis of its own. See BENCH_UX_SPEC_2026-10-08.md for the walkthrough\nthis module answers.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport json\nimport re\nimport threading\nfrom collections import Counter\nfrom datetime import datetime\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom typing import Any\n\nfrom . import cache, dossier_bridge, known_good_bridge, mes_bridge, parts_bridge, tools_kb_bridge\nfrom .errors import BadRequest\nfrom ..live import checklists as checklist_store\nfrom ..live.config import state_dir\n\ntry:\n    from . import cases_bridge\nexcept Exception:  # noqa: BLE001 -- the bench must still render without it\n    cases_bridge = None\n\ntry:\n    from . import shop_bridge\nexcept Exception:  # noqa: BLE001\n    shop_bridge = None\n\ntry:\n    from . import electrical_bridge\nexcept Exception:  # noqa: BLE001\n    electrical_bridge = None\n\ntry:\n    from ..live import ops as live_ops\nexcept Exception:  # noqa: BLE001\n    live_ops = None\n\ntry:\n    from . import scanlog_bridge\nexcept Exception:  # noqa: BLE001\n    scanlog_bridge = None\n\n\n#: Capped the same way the spec caps each bench card: 3 next actions, each\n#: with at most 3 parts and 4 tools.\n_MAX_ACTIONS = 3\n_MAX_PARTS = 3\n_MAX_TOOLS = 4\n_MAX_SHORTCUTS = 6\n_MAX_INSPECT_STEPS = 4\n\n#: Hours since the newest scan/session before the bench flags it stale\n#: (BENCH_UX_SPEC_2026-10-08.md A2) -- a stale read silently invalidates the\n#: whole checklist, so this is surfaced on the bench itself, not just in the\n#: dossier footer.\n_STALE_HOURS = 24.0\n\n#: Family key (lowercased, as ``dossier_bridge.FAMILY_STEPS``/the generic\n#: SAE-range rules spell it) -> icon registry key, for the bench card's own\n#: pictogram. Anything not listed here falls back to a generic glyph --\n#: never a 500 for a family this table doesn't know about yet.\nFAMILY_ICON: dict[str, str] = {\n    \"evap\": \"sys_evap\", \"network\": \"sys_network\", \"misfire\": \"sys_ignition\",\n    \"fuel_trim\": \"sys_fuel\", \"cooling\": \"sys_cooling\",\n    \"engine_management\": \"sys_engine_management\",\n    \"transmission_driveline\": \"sys_transmission_driveline\", \"adas\": \"sys_adas_sensors\",\n    \"chassis\": \"sys_suspension\", \"body\": \"sys_body_comfort\",\n    \"powertrain_other\": \"sys_engine_management\",\n}\n\n#: The chip colour legend rendered once below the DTC shortcut chips\n#: (BENCH_UX_SPEC_2026-10-08.md D11) -- kept here, not guessed per-chip in\n#: the template, so the legend and the chip classes can never drift apart.\n_STATUS_LEGEND = [\n    {\"label\": \"Active\", \"css\": \"v-active\"},\n    {\"label\": \"Cleared, unverified\", \"css\": \"v-cleared-unverified\"},\n]\n\n#: JOB_UX_FIXES_2026-10-08.md item 9: a single source of human labels for\n#: every raw enum this module's own output otherwise carries, so a template\n#: never has to show (or re-invent a translation for) a bare value like\n#: ``not_running`` or a verdict ``blocker`` key. Every other enum this page\n#: shows (verdict state/label, tool ``have``) is already human-labelled at\n#: its own source (dossier_bridge/tools_kb_bridge) -- this dict only covers\n#: the two that weren't: the live MES/scanner state, and the one-line\n#: action for each ``blocker`` key :func:`_fuel_gate`/the verdict compute.\nLABELS: dict[str, dict[str, str]] = {\n    \"mes_state\": {\n        \"connected\": \"Connected\", \"disconnected\": \"Disconnected\",\n        \"not_running\": \"Not running\", \"unknown\": \"Unknown\",\n    },\n    \"blocker\": {\n        \"fuel out of window\": \"Burn fuel to 15-85 %, then run a drive cycle.\",\n        \"awaiting drive cycle\": \"Run a drive cycle, then read readiness.\",\n        \"active faults\": \"Open the codes and start the first test below.\",\n    },\n}\n\n\ndef scanner_label(live_status: dict[str, Any]) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\"Connected\" / \"Not running\" / ... -- never the raw MES state enum,\n    never \"MES ?\" for an unreadable strip.\"\"\"\n    if live_status.get(\"error\"):\n        return \"Unknown\"\n    return LABELS[\"mes_state\"].get(live_status.get(\"mes_state\"), \"Unknown\")\n\n\ndef _blocker_banner(verdict: dict[str, Any]) -> dict[str, Any] | None:\n    \"\"\"The ONE banner the bench shows for \"what do I do right now\" (item\n    17): an icon, a short one-line action, and the verdict's own full\n    sentence + basis behind \"Why?\". ``None`` only when there is no\n    next_action sentence at all (should not happen in practice).","numLines":135,"startLine":1,"totalLines":890}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ad5b41e5-473d-403e-8eac-62cd28098441","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
