{"parentUuid":"c0bcb51b-089f-49a2-b952-523d669fc278","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"be0d48f1-d65f-4148-84ab-7fc82e18525f","agentId":"ae420e7134ad1bf48","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Fv4ofkGdVyAzoAK37SiPGg","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\"\"\"Checks for MIL diagnostics: the newest MES clear being recognised, and\n2\tthe ECM-commanded-MIL-vs-dash-lamp finding on Bench/Report.\n3\t\n4\tSame posture as ``cuore/tests/check_marque_port.py``/``check_tests_page.py``:\n5\t``CUORE_STATE_DIR`` and ``MES_LOG_DIR`` are both pointed at throwaway\n6\tdirectories BEFORE ``cuore`` (and therefore ``mes``) is imported, so this\n7\ttest is self-contained -- it never touches the real MultiEcuScan install or\n8\tthe real ``C:\\\\ProgramData\\\\cuore`` state, and does not depend on either\n9\tbeing present on the machine it runs on.\n10\t\n11\tThe MES-log fixture reproduces the real 2026-10-08 scenario byte-for-byte:\n12\t``SCAN_2610080920.txt`` and ``SCAN_2610080926.txt`` are copied verbatim (read\n13\t-only) from the real MultiEcuScan install when present, else from a baked-in\n14\tcopy of the same text below (so this check still runs on a machine without\n15\tthat install). A synthetic ``FESLog_2610041116...txt`` with no DTCs, dated\n16\t2026-10-04 -- *older* than the SCAN clear -- reproduces the exact condition\n17\tthat made the old clear-assessment logic miss it: the newest FES engineering\n18\tsession on file predates the newest clear, which was SCAN-only.\n19\t\n20\tThe from-car and owner-attested fixtures are narrower slices of the same two\n21\treal stores: the 2026-10-13 lines of the real ``observations.jsonl`` (MIL\n22\tcommanded on, read 20:03) when that file exists, else a baked-in equivalent\n23\tline, and one ``incidents/warning_light_seen`` owner event written through\n24\tthe real ``cuore.live.owner_events`` store API into this test's own\n25\tthrowaway state dir (never the production one).\n26\t\n27\tFour groups of checks:\n28\t  1. ``mes.workup.build()``'s ``clear_assessment`` picks the 2026-10-08\n29\t     09:20 SCAN clear (not the 2026-09-29/stale-FES-anchor date) and names\n30\t     the four DTCs it cleared.\n31\t  2. The MIL block (``cuore.services.dossier_bridge``'s new MIL section)\n32\t     carries both statements -- the ECM's and the owner's -- detects the\n33\t     mismatch, and offers the three ordered, hedged explanations, each\n34\t     paired with the mechanic_tests key that settles it. Its own text never\n35\t     uses the bare word \"cause\" or \"proven\".\n36\t  3. The three new ``mes.mechanic_tests`` entries\n37\t     (``mil_bulb_check``/``mil_request_vs_lamp``/``ipc_mil_status_read``)\n38\t     exist with a valid schema (real ``systems`` keys, allowed\n39\t     ``pass_criteria`` confidence, no numeric spec paired with UNKNOWN).\n40\t  4. Bench (``/v/{vin}``) and Report (``/v/{vin}/report``) both render 200\n41\t     and show the MIL block.\n42\t\n43\tRun:\n44\t    .venv/Scripts/python.exe cuore/tests/check_mil.py\n45\t\"\"\"\n46\t\n47\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n48\t\n49\timport os\n50\timport re\n51\timport shutil\n52\timport sys\n53\timport tempfile\n54\tfrom pathlib import Path\n55\t\n56\tos.environ[\"CUORE_STATE_DIR\"] = tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix=\"cuore-check-mil-\")\n57\tos.environ.pop(\"CUORE_AUDIT_PATH\", None)\n58\t\n59\tROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2]\n60\tsys.path.insert(0, str(ROOT))\n61\t\n62\tVIN = \"ZASFAKPN5J7B88115\"  # the Stelvio -- real VIN this whole feature was built against\n63\t\n64\t# ===========================================================================\n65\t# MES-log fixture: SCAN_2610080920/26 copied verbatim, plus a synthetic\n66\t# older FES session that reproduces the stale-anchor bug.\n67\t# ===========================================================================\n68\t\n69\t_REAL_MES_DIR = Path(r\"C:\\Program Files (x86)\\MultiEcuScan\")\n70\t_LOG_DIR = Path(tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix=\"cuore-check-mil-logs-\"))\n71\tos.environ[\"MES_LOG_DIR\"] = str(_LOG_DIR)\n72\t\n73\t# Baked-in fallback text (byte-identical in substance to the real files)\n74\t# for a machine that does not have the real MultiEcuScan install -- the\n75\t# real files are preferred when present, never modified either way.\n76\t_FALLBACK_SCAN_920 = \"\"\"Scan vehicle for available modules and check each module for errors...\n77\t\n78\tEngine / ECM\n79\tMagneti Marelli IAW 10JA CF6/EOBD Injection (2.0)\n80\tISO Code: 00 01 50 40 18\n81\tVIN code: ZASFAKPN5J7B88115\n82\tHardware number: MM10JAHW232 - Ver: 00\n83\tSoftware number: P235QB39 - Ver: 0000\n84\tErrors found:\n85\tP0456-00 - Evaporation system leak\n86\tP0455-00 - Evaporation system leak\n87\t\n88\tBody / RFHUB (Radio Frequency Hub Module)\n89\tRadio frequency hub (RFHUB) Continental\n90\tISO Code: 00 41 50 89 15\n91\tVIN code: ZASFAKPN5J7B88115\n92\tHardware number: 10161500AA - Ver: 01\n93\tSoftware number: 10307064AB - Ver: 0940\n94\tErrors found:\n95\tB1040-64 - Communication with Body Computer (BCM/NBC) - Signal/message plausibility\n96\t\n97\tOther / DASM (Driver Assistant System Module)\n98\tDriver assistant system module (DASM) radar Bosch\n99\tISO Code: 00 39 70 7E 15\n100\tVIN code: ZASFAKPN5J7B88115"}]},"uuid":"4c237167-e7aa-4ee7-a881-2ad06716d094","timestamp":"2026-10-14T12:32:56.898Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\cuore\\tests\\check_mil.py","content":"\"\"\"Checks for MIL diagnostics: the newest MES clear being recognised, and\nthe ECM-commanded-MIL-vs-dash-lamp finding on Bench/Report.\n\nSame posture as ``cuore/tests/check_marque_port.py``/``check_tests_page.py``:\n``CUORE_STATE_DIR`` and ``MES_LOG_DIR`` are both pointed at throwaway\ndirectories BEFORE ``cuore`` (and therefore ``mes``) is imported, so this\ntest is self-contained -- it never touches the real MultiEcuScan install or\nthe real ``C:\\\\ProgramData\\\\cuore`` state, and does not depend on either\nbeing present on the machine it runs on.\n\nThe MES-log fixture reproduces the real 2026-10-08 scenario byte-for-byte:\n``SCAN_2610080920.txt`` and ``SCAN_2610080926.txt`` are copied verbatim (read\n-only) from the real MultiEcuScan install when present, else from a baked-in\ncopy of the same text below (so this check still runs on a machine without\nthat install). A synthetic ``FESLog_2610041116...txt`` with no DTCs, dated\n2026-10-04 -- *older* than the SCAN clear -- reproduces the exact condition\nthat made the old clear-assessment logic miss it: the newest FES engineering\nsession on file predates the newest clear, which was SCAN-only.\n\nThe from-car and owner-attested fixtures are narrower slices of the same two\nreal stores: the 2026-10-13 lines of the real ``observations.jsonl`` (MIL\ncommanded on, read 20:03) when that file exists, else a baked-in equivalent\nline, and one ``incidents/warning_light_seen`` owner event written through\nthe real ``cuore.live.owner_events`` store API into this test's own\nthrowaway state dir (never the production one).\n\nFour groups of checks:\n  1. ``mes.workup.build()``'s ``clear_assessment`` picks the 2026-10-08\n     09:20 SCAN clear (not the 2026-09-29/stale-FES-anchor date) and names\n     the four DTCs it cleared.\n  2. The MIL block (``cuore.services.dossier_bridge``'s new MIL section)\n     carries both statements -- the ECM's and the owner's -- detects the\n     mismatch, and offers the three ordered, hedged explanations, each\n     paired with the mechanic_tests key that settles it. Its own text never\n     uses the bare word \"cause\" or \"proven\".\n  3. The three new ``mes.mechanic_tests`` entries\n     (``mil_bulb_check``/``mil_request_vs_lamp``/``ipc_mil_status_read``)\n     exist with a valid schema (real ``systems`` keys, allowed\n     ``pass_criteria`` confidence, no numeric spec paired with UNKNOWN).\n  4. Bench (``/v/{vin}``) and Report (``/v/{vin}/report``) both render 200\n     and show the MIL block.\n\nRun:\n    .venv/Scripts/python.exe cuore/tests/check_mil.py\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport os\nimport re\nimport shutil\nimport sys\nimport tempfile\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nos.environ[\"CUORE_STATE_DIR\"] = tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix=\"cuore-check-mil-\")\nos.environ.pop(\"CUORE_AUDIT_PATH\", None)\n\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2]\nsys.path.insert(0, str(ROOT))\n\nVIN = \"ZASFAKPN5J7B88115\"  # the Stelvio -- real VIN this whole feature was built against\n\n# ===========================================================================\n# MES-log fixture: SCAN_2610080920/26 copied verbatim, plus a synthetic\n# older FES session that reproduces the stale-anchor bug.\n# ===========================================================================\n\n_REAL_MES_DIR = Path(r\"C:\\Program Files (x86)\\MultiEcuScan\")\n_LOG_DIR = Path(tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix=\"cuore-check-mil-logs-\"))\nos.environ[\"MES_LOG_DIR\"] = str(_LOG_DIR)\n\n# Baked-in fallback text (byte-identical in substance to the real files)\n# for a machine that does not have the real MultiEcuScan install -- the\n# real files are preferred when present, never modified either way.\n_FALLBACK_SCAN_920 = \"\"\"Scan vehicle for available modules and check each module for errors...\n\nEngine / ECM\nMagneti Marelli IAW 10JA CF6/EOBD Injection (2.0)\nISO Code: 00 01 50 40 18\nVIN code: ZASFAKPN5J7B88115\nHardware number: MM10JAHW232 - Ver: 00\nSoftware number: P235QB39 - Ver: 0000\nErrors found:\nP0456-00 - Evaporation system leak\nP0455-00 - Evaporation system leak\n\nBody / RFHUB (Radio Frequency Hub Module)\nRadio frequency hub (RFHUB) Continental\nISO Code: 00 41 50 89 15\nVIN code: ZASFAKPN5J7B88115\nHardware number: 10161500AA - Ver: 01\nSoftware number: 10307064AB - Ver: 0940\nErrors found:\nB1040-64 - Communication with Body Computer (BCM/NBC) - Signal/message plausibility\n\nOther / DASM (Driver Assistant System Module)\nDriver assistant system module (DASM) radar Bosch\nISO Code: 00 39 70 7E 15\nVIN code: ZASFAKPN5J7B88115","numLines":100,"startLine":1,"totalLines":462}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c0bcb51b-089f-49a2-b952-523d669fc278","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
